I anchored the `--signer-workflow` match to the end of the identity, so a prefix no longer passes. I haven't compiled this or run any tests.

When the value has no `@`, the pattern now accepts the exact workflow path, optionally followed by `@` and a ref. A lookalike repository or a longer file name no longer matches. When the value contains `@`, the pattern ends right after the pinned ref, so a longer ref or an extra `@suffix` is rejected.

- **Unpinned ref suffix:** I allowed any text after the `@` in the unpinned case (`(@.+)?$`), because git ref names can legitimately contain `@`. This means an unpinned value still accepts something like `workflow.yml@refs/heads/main@extra`. If you want that rejected too, change it to `(@[^@]+)?$`.
- **Not checked:** I couldn't see how the SAN regex is applied downstream (`verification.VerifyCertExtensions` and the sigstore matcher), so I'm assuming they match the regex as written.

